<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30311" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mȳthĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυθικός</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to fables</i> or <i>myths,
				fabulous, mythic, mythical</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., a false reading for mysticus, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 53,
				54, § 184</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mȳthĭcus</span></b> , i,
			m., <i>a writer of fables</i> or <i>myths, a mythographer</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
